{"expand":"renderedFields,names,schema,operations,editmeta,changelog,versionedRepresentations","id":"74802","self":"http://172.16.10.6:8080/rest/api/2/issue/74802","key":"MOTADATA-8898","fields":{"summary":"Enhance Metric Description Availability for Multiple Categories (APM, RUM, Log, NetRoute, Flow)","issuetype":{"self":"http://172.16.10.6:8080/rest/api/2/issuetype/10300","id":"10300","description":"","iconUrl":"http://172.16.10.6:8080/secure/viewavatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10322&avatarType=issuetype","name":"Improvement","subtask":false,"avatarId":10322},"components":[{"self":"http://172.16.10.6:8080/rest/api/2/component/11400","id":"11400","name":"AIOPS"}],"description":"h4. Description:\r\n\r\nThe current implementation provides metric descriptions only for the \"Metric\" category when creating widgets. This improvement aims to extend the availability of metric descriptions to include additional categories, namely:\r\n # *APM*\r\n # *RUM*\r\n # *Log*\r\n # *NetRoute*\r\n # *Flow*\r\n\r\nBy implementing this feature, users will have access to descriptions for a broader range of metrics, making it easier to understand each metric’s significance and use case across different monitoring categories.\r\n\r\n \r\nh3. Acceptance Criteria:\r\n # {*}Metric Description Availability{*}:\r\n ** When creating a widget, descriptions must be available for the following categories:\r\n *** *APM*\r\n *** *RUM*\r\n *** *Log*\r\n *** *NetRoute*\r\n *** *Flow*\r\n ** Descriptions should display relevant information for each category’s metric (e.g., what the metric measures, how values are interpreted, and the potential root cause of anomalies).\r\n # {*}UI Update{*}:\r\n ** The widget creation interface should display a description pop-up for each metric in the above categories.\r\n ** Descriptions should be visible upon selecting a metric within the \"Metric\" dropdown.\r\n # {*}Data Source Compatibility{*}:\r\n ** Descriptions must be correctly mapped from the respective data sources and displayed consistently for each category when creating widgets.\r\n # {*}Consistency{*}:\r\n ** Descriptions across different categories should maintain a consistent format and structure for clarity.\r\n # {*}Error Handling{*}:\r\n ** If the description data for any category is missing, informing the user that the description is unavailable for that specific metric.\r\n\r\nh3. Test Cases:\r\nh4. Test Case 1: Verify Metric Descriptions for APM\r\n * {*}Preconditions{*}: User is logged into the platform and has access to create widgets.\r\n * {*}Test Steps{*}:\r\n ## Navigate to the widget creation screen.\r\n ## Select *APM* from the \"Metric\" dropdown.\r\n ## Hover over the metric to view the description.\r\n ## Verify that the description is shown correctly for the selected APM metric.\r\n * {*}Expected Result{*}: The description for the APM metric should display accurate and relevant details.\r\n\r\nh4. Test Case 2: Verify Metric Descriptions for RUM\r\n * {*}Preconditions{*}: User is logged into the platform and has access to create widgets.\r\n * {*}Test Steps{*}:\r\n ## Navigate to the widget creation screen.\r\n ## Select *RUM* from the \"Metric\" dropdown.\r\n ## Hover over the metric to view the description.\r\n ## Verify that the description is shown correctly for the selected RUM metric.\r\n * {*}Expected Result{*}: The description for the RUM metric should display accurate and relevant details.\r\n\r\nh4. Test Case 3: Verify Metric Descriptions for Log\r\n * {*}Preconditions{*}: User is logged into the platform and has access to create widgets.\r\n * {*}Test Steps{*}:\r\n ## Navigate to the widget creation screen.\r\n ## Select *Log* from the \"Metric\" dropdown.\r\n ## Hover over the metric to view the description.\r\n ## Verify that the description is shown correctly for the selected Log metric.\r\n * {*}Expected Result{*}: The description for the Log metric should display accurate and relevant details.\r\n\r\nh4. Test Case 4: Verify Metric Descriptions for NetRoute\r\n * {*}Preconditions{*}: User is logged into the platform and has access to create widgets.\r\n * {*}Test Steps{*}:\r\n ## Navigate to the widget creation screen.\r\n ## Select *NetRoute* from the \"Metric\" dropdown.\r\n ## Hover over the metric to view the description.\r\n ## Verify that the description is shown correctly for the selected NetRoute metric.\r\n * {*}Expected Result{*}: The description for the NetRoute metric should display accurate and relevant details.\r\n\r\nh4. Test Case 5: Verify Metric Descriptions for Flow\r\n * {*}Preconditions{*}: User is logged into the platform and has access to create widgets.\r\n * {*}Test Steps{*}:\r\n ## Navigate to the widget creation screen.\r\n ## Select *Flow* from the \"Metric\" dropdown.\r\n ## Hover over the metric to view the description.\r\n ## Verify that the description is shown correctly for the selected Flow metric.\r\n * {*}Expected Result{*}: The description for the Flow metric should display accurate and relevant details.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nFigma:\r\n\r\n[https://www.figma.com/proto/DPReGBjeIv7nogzeNs9Uel/Settings?page-id=0%3A1&node-id=24784-199311&p=f&viewport=-58%2C959%2C0.02&t=2jtwAQPotHGzDYU9-1&scaling=scale-down-width&content-scaling=fixed&starting-point-node-id=632%3A36804]\r\n\r\n ","comment":{"comments":[{"self":"http://172.16.10.6:8080/rest/api/2/issue/74802/comment/83510","id":"83510","author":{"self":"http://172.16.10.6:8080/rest/api/2/user?username=umang.sharma","name":"umang.sharma","key":"JIRAUSER10183","emailAddress":"umang.sharma@motadata.com","avatarUrls":{"48x48":"http://172.16.10.6:8080/secure/useravatar?ownerId=JIRAUSER10183&avatarId=10900","24x24":"http://172.16.10.6:8080/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=JIRAUSER10183&avatarId=10900","16x16":"http://172.16.10.6:8080/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=JIRAUSER10183&avatarId=10900","32x32":"http://172.16.10.6:8080/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=JIRAUSER10183&avatarId=10900"},"displayName":"Umang Sharma","active":true,"timeZone":"Asia/Kolkata"},"body":"[~bhavin.gorecha]  seed.json is not as per the format of the backend json for metric description and it will only work for performance metric \r\n[^Linux.json]please refer this.. ","updateAuthor":{"self":"http://172.16.10.6:8080/rest/api/2/user?username=umang.sharma","name":"umang.sharma","key":"JIRAUSER10183","emailAddress":"umang.sharma@motadata.com","avatarUrls":{"48x48":"http://172.16.10.6:8080/secure/useravatar?ownerId=JIRAUSER10183&avatarId=10900","24x24":"http://172.16.10.6:8080/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=JIRAUSER10183&avatarId=10900","16x16":"http://172.16.10.6:8080/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=JIRAUSER10183&avatarId=10900","32x32":"http://172.16.10.6:8080/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=JIRAUSER10183&avatarId=10900"},"displayName":"Umang Sharma","active":true,"timeZone":"Asia/Kolkata"},"created":"2026-05-18T12:25:19.016+0530","updated":"2026-05-18T12:25:19.016+0530"},{"self":"http://172.16.10.6:8080/rest/api/2/issue/74802/comment/83623","id":"83623","author":{"self":"http://172.16.10.6:8080/rest/api/2/user?username=shivani.shah","name":"shivani.shah","key":"JIRAUSER10169","emailAddress":"shivani.shah@motadata.com","avatarUrls":{"48x48":"http://172.16.10.6:8080/secure/useravatar?ownerId=JIRAUSER10169&avatarId=10611","24x24":"http://172.16.10.6:8080/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=JIRAUSER10169&avatarId=10611","16x16":"http://172.16.10.6:8080/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=JIRAUSER10169&avatarId=10611","32x32":"http://172.16.10.6:8080/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=JIRAUSER10169&avatarId=10611"},"displayName":"Shivani Shah","active":true,"timeZone":"Asia/Kolkata"},"body":"[~umang.sharma] Please review the test cases for the Log and Flow modules and let me know if there are any missing scenarios.\r\n\r\n[^metric_testcases_simple.csv]\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n ","updateAuthor":{"self":"http://172.16.10.6:8080/rest/api/2/user?username=shivani.shah","name":"shivani.shah","